Great question 👍 — this is an advanced UI trick in Power Apps because there is no built-in “freeze pane” like Excel.

But we can simulate it perfectly 👇


---

🎯 GOAL (Like Excel Freeze Pane)

[Fixed] Supplier | Code || Scroll → M1R | M5R | D3R | Q4R

✔ Supplier + Code stay visible
✔ Only questions scroll horizontally


---

🔥 SOLUTION: SPLIT INTO 2 SECTIONS

👉 Instead of 1 table, we create 2 synchronized layouts


---

🧩 FINAL STRUCTURE

MainContainer (Horizontal)

   ├── LeftContainer (FIXED)
   │     ├── Header (Supplier | Code)
   │     └── Gallery_Suppliers_Left
   │
   └── RightScrollContainer (SCROLLABLE)
         ├── Header (Questions)
         └── Gallery_Suppliers_Right


---

🧩 STEP 1: MAIN CONTAINER

Direction = LayoutDirection.Horizontal


---

🧩 STEP 2: LEFT SIDE (FROZEN COLUMNS)

LeftContainer

Width = 270   // 150 + 120


---

Header (Left)

Supplier | Code


---

Gallery_Suppliers_Left

Items:

Filter(
    'SE Supplier List',
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
)


---

Inside row:

Supplier Name → Width = 150
Supplier Code → Width = 120


---

🧩 STEP 3: RIGHT SIDE (SCROLLABLE)

RightScrollContainer

OverflowX = Overflow.Scroll
OverflowY = Overflow.Hidden
Align = Align.Start
Width = Parent.Width - 270


---

🧩 STEP 4: HEADER (QUESTIONS)

Gallery_Header

Items = colQuestions
TemplateSize = 110
Width = CountRows(colQuestions) * 110


---

🧩 STEP 5: ROWS (QUESTIONS)

Gallery_Suppliers_Right

SAME Items as Left:

Gallery_Suppliers_Left.Items


---

Inside row → Gallery_Question_H

Items = colQuestions
TemplateSize = 110
Width = CountRows(colQuestions) * 110


---

🧩 STEP 6: RADIO BUTTON

Items = Sequence(ThisItem.'Max Score')
Layout = Layout.Horizontal
Width = Parent.TemplateWidth


---

🔗 STEP 7: SYNC ROW HEIGHT (IMPORTANT)

Set BOTH galleries:

TemplateSize = 60   // same value


---

🧠 WHY THIS WORKS

LeftContainer = fixed (no scroll)
RightContainer = scrollable

→ Looks like frozen columns


